capability publish-estate-live-observation
intent: Publish executions into the estate's live observation channel, the publish/subscribe channel every capability execution in the estate is published into, whether it was admitted as a run or answered within a request. A batch may hold several executions' events: each event names its execution, or the batch's execution names it. For each event, in the order written and at the channel position the hosting facade reserved for it, the answer is its observer record and frame and its effect on the channel's run windows. The record is the legacy observer's {seq, observationKey, receivedAt, kind, runId, api, glyph, cls, text, payload}: run.started and run.exited are the execution's run-start and run-end, whose payload is the record itself with at, pid or exitCode and apiRunId; every other event is an observation whose payload is the event's own; api names the event (eventId, cursor, kind, occurredAt, recordedAt, rootExecutionId), the execution and its capability; glyph, cls and text are the observer's summary, without its shape notes. The frame is id: <seq> and one data line. The run window effect: the start opens the execution's window, the end closes it, a graph capture names a graph the run captured. The facade appends each frame to the channel and applies each effect as answered; subscribers are served by subscribe-estate-live-observation and select-estate-live-observation.
outcome: publish-estate-live-observation-result.v1: one publication per event, in order, each {seq, frame, window}
inquiry: How does this execution appear on the estate live observation channel?
input contract publish-estate-live-observation-request.v1 {"type":"object","required":["channel","events"],"properties":{"channel":{"type":"string"},"execution":{"type":"object","required":["executionId"],"properties":{"executionId":{"type":"string"},"capability":{"type":"object"}}},"events":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["seq","receivedAt","event"],"properties":{"execution":{"type":"object","required":["executionId"],"properties":{"executionId":{"type":"string"},"capability":{"type":"object"}}}}}}}}
output contract publish-estate-live-observation-result.v1 {"type":"object","required":["contractId","publications"]}
cli display outcome as json
scenario publish-estate-live-observation root terminal
given: the channel, an execution with its capability, and a batch of its events at their reserved channel positions
when: each event is attributed to the execution, summarized and framed as the observer's record
then: the outcome is one publication per event, in order, with its frame and its run window effect
operation publish-estate-live-observation.publish kind invoke-port port publish-estate-live-observation-publish
platform bind publish-estate-live-observation-publish
platform: sda-authority-transformation-port.v1
